WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:02.324 --> 00:00:02.865
Good morning.

00:00:05.480 --> 00:00:06.740
My name is Lulu Li.

00:00:06.740 --> 00:00:10.130
I'm a fifth-year PhD student
at the Nuclear Science

00:00:10.130 --> 00:00:13.410
and Engineering
Department here at MIT.

00:00:13.410 --> 00:00:16.630
As [INAUDIBLE] mentioned that
of the various things that

00:00:16.630 --> 00:00:19.540
make this place home to me,
I'm particularly honored

00:00:19.540 --> 00:00:22.490
to be the co-president
for ACME, which

00:00:22.490 --> 00:00:26.490
stands for Academy of
Courageous Minority Engineers.

00:00:26.490 --> 00:00:30.790
We're a student group
generously supported under ODGE.

00:00:30.790 --> 00:00:34.100
I have the honor here to
be your master of ceremony

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.820
today for this event.

00:00:35.820 --> 00:00:39.354
Please join me in thanking the
MIT Gospel Choir one more time.

00:00:39.354 --> 00:00:42.296
[APPLAUSE]

00:00:49.060 --> 00:00:53.135
I would like to introduce
Reverend Rahsaan Hall, who will

00:00:53.135 --> 00:00:55.150
lead this morning's invocation.

00:00:55.150 --> 00:00:57.904
[APPLAUSE]

00:01:03.170 --> 00:01:05.740
Good morning.

00:01:05.740 --> 00:01:08.380
Out of respect for all
faiths and religions,

00:01:08.380 --> 00:01:10.490
let us come together
collectively

00:01:10.490 --> 00:01:15.750
and center ourselves
in a word of prayer.

00:01:15.750 --> 00:01:21.470
Great and marvelous creator,
you are our inspiration.

00:01:21.470 --> 00:01:25.400
You have been our sustainer
in times of trouble.

00:01:25.400 --> 00:01:30.990
In those wilderness experiences,
you have held us in your hand.

00:01:30.990 --> 00:01:34.160
We acknowledge your presence
in all that will be done

00:01:34.160 --> 00:01:37.530
and said in this place.

00:01:37.530 --> 00:01:40.170
You are our inspiration.

00:01:40.170 --> 00:01:44.050
In times long forgotten,
you shielded us from harm,

00:01:44.050 --> 00:01:47.970
creating pathways where
none existed before.

00:01:47.970 --> 00:01:50.865
We humble ourselves before you.

00:01:50.865 --> 00:01:53.900
You are our inspiration.

00:01:53.900 --> 00:01:58.280
In the face of oppression and
the unjust exercise of power,

00:01:58.280 --> 00:02:00.960
you have reminded
us that whoever

00:02:00.960 --> 00:02:04.730
closes their ear to the
cry of the poor will

00:02:04.730 --> 00:02:08.350
themselves call out
and not be answered.

00:02:08.350 --> 00:02:11.810
And we endeavor to listen
with not only open ears,

00:02:11.810 --> 00:02:14.340
but open hearts as well.

00:02:14.340 --> 00:02:17.520
You are our inspiration.

00:02:17.520 --> 00:02:21.330
To be rooted and grounded
in your divine love,

00:02:21.330 --> 00:02:25.250
that we might yield our
power to the powerless,

00:02:25.250 --> 00:02:27.490
so they may be strong.

00:02:27.490 --> 00:02:31.760
Keep us forever in
your path, we pray.

00:02:31.760 --> 00:02:33.310
Amen.

